    "result_text": "There's one test class and it passes. Build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`:\n\n1. **New function** `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 logs to the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`), emitting the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`. It takes the persisted `@Val Owner`, so all three fields are populated.\n\n2. **Wired it into the pipeline** in `owners.POST.yml` as a new `audit` step placed *after* `save` (so the DB-generated id is available) and before `respond`, keeping it under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors:\n   ```\n   save \u2192 audit \u2192 respond\n   ```\n\nThe audit line (e.g. `owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-17`) contains each of the three values as substrings, which is what the `AcceptanceTest` (`coreLogsAuditOnCreate`) asserts via `AuditLogCapture`. `registrationDate` serializes identically to `LocalDate.toString()` (ISO `yyyy-MM-dd`), matching the value the test reads back from the owner JSON.\n\nFull test suite: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.",
